-Start you out with a water as well?
-No, two shots, no water.

230
00:10:21,329 --> 00:10:23,331
But I have to wake up so early for--

231
00:10:23,414 --> 00:10:24,790
You'll be fine, I promise.

232
00:10:26,334 --> 00:10:28,544
This is one of our signature cocktails
turned into a shot.

233
00:10:28,627 --> 00:10:29,712
It's called the La Brea.

234
00:10:30,588 --> 00:10:33,174
Cheers to having me on your side.

235
00:10:33,424 --> 00:10:34,508
[Chrishell] I love that.

236
00:10:34,592 --> 00:10:36,385
I look forward 
to taking you under my wing.

237
00:10:36,677 --> 00:10:39,388
Uh! Cheers. That's so sweet. Thanks.

238
00:10:43,434 --> 00:10:49,815
-That was surprisingly easy.
-That was like if a salad was a shot.

239
00:10:50,733 --> 00:10:53,444
So what are your thoughts 
on dinner the other night?

240
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:57,782
Well, it was nice to see everybody
outside of the office.

241
00:10:57,865 --> 00:11:00,284
-Yeah, it always is.
-There were a few awkward moments.

242
00:11:00,368 --> 00:11:03,704
So, you actually knew before I did
that Maya was pregnant.

243
00:11:03,954 --> 00:11:06,957
I know... Honestly, though,
it was by accident.

244
00:11:07,041 --> 00:11:08,709
I know it was an honest mistake,

245
00:11:08,793 --> 00:11:13,547
but just be careful next time because
we're a really small group of people.

246
00:11:13,631 --> 00:11:17,968
So secrets and things get out
and it causes explosions.

247
00:11:18,052 --> 00:11:19,720
Okay. I have no defense.

248
00:11:19,804 --> 00:11:23,182
-I know.
-I literally just still feel so bad.

249
00:11:23,265 --> 00:11:24,725
Just live and learn.

250
00:11:25,434 --> 00:11:29,230
But it seemed like Davina was
really calling you out.

251
00:11:29,939 --> 00:11:33,401
It's frustrating that people are talking--

252
00:11:33,484 --> 00:11:36,320
You did ask me about, like,
does he pay for stuff.

253
00:11:36,404 --> 00:11:40,116
Yeah, and I think it's because
you don't really know. You know?

254
00:11:40,533 --> 00:11:41,367
Okay.

255
00:11:41,701 --> 00:11:43,869
You know what it is?
It was just interesting.

256
00:11:43,953 --> 00:11:48,999
She kind of brought it up in conversation,
and so I asked her a few questions,

257
00:11:49,083 --> 00:11:52,044
'cause I was trying to understand where 
everybody's concern was coming from.

258
00:11:52,128 --> 00:11:54,463
So I said, 
"Well, is she paying for everything?"

259
00:11:54,547 --> 00:11:56,882
And she was like, "I don't think so."

260
00:11:56,966 --> 00:11:59,969
So I was like, "Okay." 
But then, in front of Mary,

261
00:12:00,052 --> 00:12:02,263
she was kind of like,
"Well, Chrishell said..."

262
00:12:02,346 --> 00:12:05,057
and I was like, "I never said that."
First of all, I don't know them,

263
00:12:05,141 --> 00:12:06,475
so I wouldn't say that.

264
00:12:06,559 --> 00:12:08,602
When Davina threw me under the bus,

265
00:12:08,686 --> 00:12:11,355
I'm not gonna be that person
that just doesn't say something.

266
00:12:11,522 --> 00:12:14,483
So here's the thing
that I love about Davina,

267
00:12:14,567 --> 00:12:17,319
is she's a lot like me. She's no bullshit.

268
00:12:17,403 --> 00:12:19,822
Like, you know, she will say it how it is.

269
00:12:19,905 --> 00:12:23,784
So she's one person 
that you probably wanna be friends with.

270
00:12:24,869 --> 00:12:27,788
If you don't own up 
to the things that you say,

271
00:12:27,872 --> 00:12:30,207
you're gonna get in trouble
in this brokerage. It's small.

272
00:12:30,291 --> 00:12:33,502
So you need to not get your feelings hurt

273
00:12:33,586 --> 00:12:36,005
and don't think that you're being
thrown under the bus

274
00:12:36,088 --> 00:12:38,966
because you're being called out
on something that you've said.

275
00:12:39,049 --> 00:12:41,886
She can't be meek
and she has to be stronger.

276
00:12:41,969 --> 00:12:44,430
And if she's not, she's not gonna last.

277
00:12:44,513 --> 00:12:48,142
As long as you know don't... with me...

278
00:12:48,225 --> 00:12:50,269
I would say, don't... with Davina,

279
00:12:50,352 --> 00:12:52,188
and be careful around Mary.

280
00:12:52,855 --> 00:12:53,814
You'll do fine.

281
00:12:53,898 --> 00:12:57,526
I know you have a tough exterior, but you
seem like a teddy bear on the inside.

282
00:12:57,610 --> 00:13:00,029
I'm bound and determined to see it.

283
00:13:00,112 --> 00:13:02,198
No. I'm a total teddy bear.

284
00:13:02,281 --> 00:13:03,449
I can see it.

285
00:13:03,532 --> 00:13:06,702
I was, like, the nerd in high school.
Everyone made fun of me.

286
00:13:06,786 --> 00:13:08,662
Like everyone said
I would go nowhere in life.

287
00:13:08,746 --> 00:13:10,456
-I swear to God I could cry right now.
-What?

288
00:13:10,539 --> 00:13:11,790
No, I swear to God.

289
00:13:12,249 --> 00:13:14,335
-No! I'm like, "Why am I crying?"
-No.

290
00:13:14,418 --> 00:13:17,046
No, but, seriously, I am a teddy bear.
I really am.

291
00:13:17,129 --> 00:13:20,424
I'm also, like, 
very just to the point and honest,

292
00:13:20,508 --> 00:13:23,677
and sometimes
that comes across, like, the wrong way.

293
00:13:23,761 --> 00:13:25,513
And I hate that. That's not my intention,

294
00:13:25,596 --> 00:13:27,640
'cause people don't have
a sense of humor.

295
00:13:28,516 --> 00:13:30,184
What were you like in high school?
I'm curious.

296
00:13:30,559 --> 00:13:32,102
I come from poverty.

297
00:13:32,186 --> 00:13:34,396
So I was, like, the smelly kid,

298
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:37,900
'cause sometimes I didn't have
running water. Now, I'm not gonna cry.

299
00:13:38,317 --> 00:13:40,945
Um... But, um, I really relate to you,

300
00:13:41,028 --> 00:13:42,863
because it's one of those things

301
00:13:42,947 --> 00:13:46,075
where it's like people 
would never assume that now

302
00:13:46,158 --> 00:13:49,411
'cause I've worked so hard
to get away from that.

303
00:13:50,663 --> 00:13:55,084
It's crazy. Like, you really don't know
what people have been through,

304
00:13:55,167 --> 00:13:57,670
and I think you're so strong. I really do.

305
00:13:57,753 --> 00:14:01,715
But I'm just really happy
that you joined our brokerage,

306
00:14:01,799 --> 00:14:04,510
-and that, um--
-You'll keep me in line.

307
00:14:04,593 --> 00:14:07,388
If I give you a hard time, I'm sorry.
It's not my intention,

308
00:14:07,471 --> 00:14:10,182
I just want you to be professional
and I want people to love you.

309
00:14:10,266 --> 00:14:13,018
So, that's my only intention for you,
I promise.

310
00:14:13,102 --> 00:14:15,563
-I feel a hug coming on.
-I feel a hug coming on!

311
00:14:15,646 --> 00:14:17,982
Come here. Aw, that's so nice.

312
00:14:18,065 --> 00:14:20,943
-Aw. I love--
-Thank you so much for inviting me out.

313
00:14:21,026 --> 00:14:22,862
-[Christine] Of course.
-[Chrishell] It's been so nice.

314
00:14:22,945 --> 00:14:23,904
[Christine] Of course.

315
00:14:24,363 --> 00:14:27,366
♪ Ooh, on top of the world ♪ 

316
00:14:32,913 --> 00:14:34,790
♪ On top of the world ♪ 

317
00:14:35,457 --> 00:14:37,585
[Brandon] So they built 
all the way up to the hillside.

318
00:14:37,668 --> 00:14:39,461
As high as they could, yes.

319
00:14:39,545 --> 00:14:41,255
And it doesn't look as tall
from down here,

320
00:14:41,338 --> 00:14:44,300
but I swear it's insane.
So look at the view.

321
00:14:44,383 --> 00:14:47,303
This is not even anything compared
to what else you're gonna see.

322
00:14:47,386 --> 00:14:49,638
I'm looking at those power lines,
and I know you said--

323
00:14:49,722 --> 00:14:52,641
Well, you won't be looking at them
for very long, 'cause they'll be dropped.

324
00:14:52,933 --> 00:14:55,895
He's spending half a million dollars
to drop the powerlines.

325
00:14:56,562 --> 00:14:58,230
[Heather] 
It's around 20,000 square feet...

326
00:14:58,314 --> 00:14:59,565
-Okay.
-...which is giant.

327
00:14:59,648 --> 00:15:02,568
And this is actually 
the last home of this size

328
00:15:02,651 --> 00:15:04,320
that is allowed to be built in the Hills.

329
00:15:04,403 --> 00:15:06,488
The city shut it down. So this is it.

330
00:15:08,949 --> 00:15:13,329
So basically when you walk in, on this
side, there's a full gym, two saunas--

331
00:15:13,412 --> 00:15:16,248
-Two saunas? Why would you need two?
-I mean, why wouldn't you?

332
00:15:16,498 --> 00:15:18,459
Atrium with a palm tree.

333
00:15:18,959 --> 00:15:21,712
-That sells it right there.
-Who has a palm tree in their home?

334
00:15:21,962 --> 00:15:24,673
And there's a beautiful movie theater.

335
00:15:24,757 --> 00:15:26,925
-This is all pool right?
-The pool, yeah.

336
00:15:27,009 --> 00:15:29,762
The pool basically wraps 
around the whole house,

337
00:15:29,845 --> 00:15:32,264
so I think that you should get in
and take a little swim.

338
00:15:33,390 --> 00:15:36,393
Oh, I can feel it already.
Are you sure you don't want to get in?

339
00:15:36,477 --> 00:15:38,312
I've decided not to swim today.

340
00:15:38,395 --> 00:15:41,523
You could have rafts in here
and float around like a lazy river.

341
00:15:41,607 --> 00:15:43,609
-[Brandon] A giant swan!
-[Heather] There you go.

342
00:15:43,734 --> 00:15:45,986
-How big is this?
-A hundred and fifty feet long.

343
00:15:46,528 --> 00:15:48,948
Have you ever been 
inside of a pool that big?

344
00:15:49,031 --> 00:15:52,159
At a hotel, yes,
but on a private property, no.

345
00:15:52,660 --> 00:15:56,455
Hello, this is a huge listing.
It'd be the biggest one I've ever had

346
00:15:56,538 --> 00:15:58,791
and the biggest one
at the Oppenheim Group.

347
00:15:58,874 --> 00:16:00,751
It would make a huge statement for me.

348
00:16:00,834 --> 00:16:03,587
So tell your client this is
the last one of this size.

349
00:16:03,671 --> 00:16:05,506
You better jump on it.
It's gonna go quick.

350
00:16:05,589 --> 00:16:08,175
We can do a really good
housewarming party if he buys it.

351
00:16:08,258 --> 00:16:11,053
-Or when. Let's say when he buys.
-Yes!

352
00:16:11,136 --> 00:16:12,429
Let's do it.

353
00:16:13,555 --> 00:16:16,266
♪ You've got to let it go ♪ 

354
00:16:16,350 --> 00:16:18,978
♪ You've got to live out loud ♪ 

355
00:16:19,061 --> 00:16:21,647
♪ You've got to let them know ♪ 

356
00:16:21,730 --> 00:16:23,732
♪ We're flying up above the clouds... ♪ 

357
00:16:24,233 --> 00:16:27,111
-Me so hungry.
-Oh, I know. Me too.

358
00:16:30,739 --> 00:16:33,867
Oh, my God, I'm starving.

359
00:16:34,284 --> 00:16:37,037
Yeah. Can't wait to get my coffee.

360
00:16:37,287 --> 00:16:38,622
We haven't seen each other a lot.

361
00:16:38,789 --> 00:16:40,082
-You've been really busy.
-I know.

362
00:16:40,207 --> 00:16:41,792
-It's ridiculous.
-Your work, yeah.

363
00:16:41,875 --> 00:16:44,503
I think we saw each other more
when we weren't living together.

364
00:16:44,586 --> 00:16:46,422
[chuckles] Yeah.

365
00:16:46,505 --> 00:16:48,298
[Mary chuckles] This is getting...

366
00:16:48,590 --> 00:16:50,926
-[Romain] Yeah, you're working so much.
-Jeez. It's tough.

367
00:16:51,010 --> 00:16:52,845
Good morning, welcome to Fig.

368
00:16:52,928 --> 00:16:54,763
Hi, my name is Chris.
I'll be your server today.

369
00:16:54,847 --> 00:16:56,306
-Thank you.
-Some menus for you.

370
00:16:56,390 --> 00:16:57,433
All right. Thank you.

371
00:16:57,516 --> 00:17:01,186
I think I'm gonna do 
an egg white omelette with avocado.

372
00:17:01,270 --> 00:17:02,104
[Chris] Perfect.

373
00:17:02,187 --> 00:17:05,399
I'm going to get, like, a toast
with juice and coffee.

374
00:17:05,482 --> 00:17:07,484
-[Chris] Sounds good.
-Cool. Thank you.

375
00:17:09,028 --> 00:17:12,114
-How was your morning?
-It was good. Busy. Yeah.

376
00:17:12,197 --> 00:17:14,908
You know that house
that I showed the other day...

377
00:17:15,284 --> 00:17:18,829
-The one you really liked?
-...on Fremont? Yeah.

378
00:17:18,912 --> 00:17:20,914
-I really want you to see it.
-Yeah?

379
00:17:20,998 --> 00:17:22,166
It's so cool.

380
00:17:22,249 --> 00:17:28,797
It feels homey...
and just hip at the same time.

381
00:17:28,881 --> 00:17:31,050
Yeah? What did he say about it?

382
00:17:31,467 --> 00:17:33,886
-Are they gonna make an offer?
-She likes it.

383
00:17:33,969 --> 00:17:36,430
-She likes it a lot.
-[Chris] A latte for you, miss.

384
00:17:36,513 --> 00:17:39,058
-[Mary] Thank you.
-[Chris] For you, sir, whole milk latte.

385
00:17:39,141 --> 00:17:40,309
[Mary] Thank you.

386
00:17:40,434 --> 00:17:45,272
We should probably start thinking about
what we're gonna do once we get married,

387
00:17:45,355 --> 00:17:47,733
-like where we're gonna live.
-Mm-hmm.

388
00:17:47,816 --> 00:17:53,322
Do we want to keep 
the same kind of, like, condo...

389
00:17:53,405 --> 00:17:54,698
-situation...
-I don't know.

390
00:17:54,782 --> 00:17:57,367
...or do we want a house?

391
00:17:57,451 --> 00:18:03,290
Because, after seeing that Fremont house,
I'm, like, that's what I want. [chuckles]

392
00:18:03,582 --> 00:18:04,917
Um, I've thought about it.

393
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:09,213
I don't know if it would be better for us
to just keep living where we are.

394
00:18:10,172 --> 00:18:11,090
Yeah.

395
00:18:12,341 --> 00:18:13,217
Yeah.

396
00:18:13,300 --> 00:18:15,469
But we need to have
a couple extra bedrooms,

397
00:18:15,552 --> 00:18:17,679
for whenever Austin comes out to visit

398
00:18:17,763 --> 00:18:19,598
-or whenever your parents come.
-Mm-hmm.

399
00:18:19,681 --> 00:18:24,812
So we need at least two bedrooms,
maybe three so we can have an office.

400
00:18:24,895 --> 00:18:26,021
[chuckles]

401
00:18:27,272 --> 00:18:28,899
Do you want to get a bigger place?

402
00:18:28,982 --> 00:18:32,861
Do you think it's important for us
to have more room, or do you just...

403
00:18:33,654 --> 00:18:34,488
I don't know.

404
00:18:35,739 --> 00:18:40,786
I also will see,
I have to do, you know, more...

405
00:18:40,869 --> 00:18:43,622
-Maintenance and stuff on it. I know.
-Yeah. More, I guess.

406
00:18:43,705 --> 00:18:45,916
I mean, it doesn't need to be huge, but--

407
00:18:45,999 --> 00:18:49,169
No, that's for sure, I mean...
I don't know.

408
00:18:49,253 --> 00:18:50,796
-I guess--
-What style do you like?

409
00:18:50,879 --> 00:18:52,339
You know, with a hot tub.

410
00:18:53,173 --> 00:18:54,800
-With a hot tub?
-Yeah.

411
00:18:54,883 --> 00:18:56,468
What? [laughs]

412
00:18:56,552 --> 00:18:58,095
A hot tub? Okay.

413
00:18:58,345 --> 00:19:01,139
Or a pool or I don't know,
but something like that.

414
00:19:01,223 --> 00:19:04,184
Well, I mean, you have to have a house,
it's cool, no?

415
00:19:04,268 --> 00:19:05,185
Yeah.

416
00:19:06,562 --> 00:19:08,438
If you're all set,
I'll have the check dropped.

417
00:19:08,522 --> 00:19:09,898
-Perfect, thank you.
-My pleasure.

418
00:19:09,982 --> 00:19:12,276
-Let me know if you need anything.
-[Romain] Thank you.

419
00:19:12,818 --> 00:19:14,194
[gasps] I don't have my--

420
00:19:14,862 --> 00:19:16,155
Do you have your wallet?

421
00:19:16,238 --> 00:19:17,156
Give me your card.

422
00:19:18,323 --> 00:19:20,409
I don't have my card with me, baby.

423
00:19:20,492 --> 00:19:23,537
-It's in my car.
-Uh-huh. I see how you are.

424
00:19:24,371 --> 00:19:25,455
[Romain chuckles]

425
00:19:25,539 --> 00:19:27,958
-Babe, I swear I don't have it.
-Mm-hmm.

426
00:19:28,750 --> 00:19:30,043
I really don't have my wallet.

427
00:19:30,127 --> 00:19:34,131
Put a ring on the finger and now you're
like, "Baby, you can pay, right?"

428
00:19:34,214 --> 00:19:36,592
I forgot my card. [laughs]

429
00:19:36,675 --> 00:19:39,178
Yeah, right. I'm looking in there
when we get back.

430
00:19:40,596 --> 00:19:42,723
-Yeah!
-I'm joking.

431
00:19:46,518 --> 00:19:48,979
-This is cute.
-Yeah, this is super cute.

432
00:19:49,062 --> 00:19:51,940
So, you know, 
this area called, like, Hollywood Dell.

433
00:19:52,024 --> 00:19:56,069
East Hollywood Hills, 
like old, classic, Spanish.

434
00:19:56,904 --> 00:19:59,406
Yeah, it's pretty cool,
they remodeled the whole property.

435
00:20:01,533 --> 00:20:03,785
[Chrishell] I can't wait 
to see inside. This is pretty.

436
00:20:03,869 --> 00:20:06,997
-Yeah, super nice. Very Spanish.
-[Chrishell] I like all the greenery.

437
00:20:09,499 --> 00:20:13,754
All right. Welcome 
to our Spanish revival new listing.

438
00:20:13,837 --> 00:20:16,215
It's not your typical, 
like, open floor plan.

439
00:20:16,298 --> 00:20:17,925
It's an amazing house.

440
00:20:22,221 --> 00:20:24,932
So you kind of know the stats, right?
You have the setup sheet.

441
00:20:25,140 --> 00:20:30,354
Why don't... I'm gonna be your client
and you're just gonna show me the house.

442
00:20:30,437 --> 00:20:32,189
Oh, a little role play.

443
00:20:32,898 --> 00:20:36,026
If I'm a buyer and I'm walking 
into a Sunday open house

444
00:20:36,109 --> 00:20:37,986
and I'm asking the agent questions,

445
00:20:38,070 --> 00:20:39,821
they better know the answers.

446
00:20:39,905 --> 00:20:42,199
Size, price, details.

447
00:20:42,282 --> 00:20:45,327
So I wanted to test Chrishell
and play with her a little bit

448
00:20:45,410 --> 00:20:49,623
just in case she will see the open house
on Sunday when I cannot be there.

449
00:20:49,706 --> 00:20:54,002
So this is a beautiful Spanish home
and it's very unique.

450
00:20:54,378 --> 00:20:56,588
Um, you know,
you won't find this everywhere.

451
00:20:56,672 --> 00:20:59,591
A lot of the homes around here
are very modern.

452
00:21:00,175 --> 00:21:03,011
But that's the thing.
When I sent you the listings that I want,

453
00:21:03,095 --> 00:21:06,056
I wanted a modern house, so why
did you bring me to the Spanish one?

454
00:21:06,515 --> 00:21:08,850
-Oh.
-So can we just leave?

455
00:21:08,934 --> 00:21:11,270
-I'm kidding. I'm giving you a hard time.
-My God! [laughs]

456
00:21:11,353 --> 00:21:14,398
I'm kidding, okay.
This is beautiful. All right.

457
00:21:14,648 --> 00:21:17,109
Shit, you really got me. [laughs]

458
00:21:17,192 --> 00:21:18,402
